**sum(...numbers)**

Write `sum(...numbers)`: add up any number of arguments. `sum()` is 0.

```js
function sum(numbers) {
  // TODO
  return 0;
}
```

notes.back:
// Why: `...numbers` gathers all arguments into a real array. reduce needs the initial
// value 0, or an empty array throws a TypeError.
// Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Functions/rest_parameters
function sum(...numbers) {
  return numbers.reduce((total, n) => total + n, 0);
}
